QA Dashboard - Multi-Team Workspace Architecture
Background
Our QA Dashboard was originally built for a single internal team. After logging in through LDAP, every authenticated user could see all Groups, Projects, Releases, Defects, Test Runs, etc.
This worked because only one team was using the application.
Now the application is being rolled out to multiple teams across the organization.
This introduces a major security and usability problem.
Current Problems
Every LDAP authenticated user can see every configured project.
Teams should never see another team's Jira/QTest configuration.
Teams should only access their own dashboard.
New users currently have no onboarding flow.
Project configuration currently requires backend/API support instead of being completely self-service.
The application is not designed as an enterprise multi-tenant SaaS product.
Goal
Transform QA Dashboard into a multi-workspace enterprise application where every team owns its own isolated workspace.
Each workspace contains:
App Code
Jira Issue Key
QTest ID
Jira Token
QTest Token
Dashboard Data
Releases
Bugs
Test Runs
Reports




No workspace can access another workspace's data.
